(rest_ext: A Generic REST API Extension for DuckDB) Tj
0.070 0.220 0.380 rg
54.00 708.00 504.00 1.60 re f
/F2 13.50 Tf
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 677.00 Tm
(Executive Summary) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
54.00 656.00 504.00 0.75 re f
/F1 10.30 Tf
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 637.00 Tm
(rest_ext is a DuckDB extension that lets any REST API be queried with plain SQL. A user ATTACHes an API) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 623.00 Tm
(the same way they would ATTACH a Postgres or MySQL database, and every endpoint becomes a callable) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 609.00 Tm
(table function returning rows whose schema is inferred automatically from the API's own JSON responses. No) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 595.00 Tm
(connectors, no per-API code, no ETL scripts - configuration alone is enough to turn a REST API into a) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 581.00 Tm
(SQL-queryable data source.) Tj
/F2 13.50 Tf
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 551.00 Tm
(Problem) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
54.00 530.00 504.00 0.75 re f
/F1 10.30 Tf
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 511.00 Tm
(DuckDB already has first-class scanners for relational databases \(postgres_scanner, mysql_scanner\) and for) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 497.00 Tm
(flat files \(read_json, read_csv, read_parquet\). It has no equivalent for the REST APIs that a large share of) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 483.00 Tm
(real-world "cost and usage" data actually lives behind - cloud billing APIs, SaaS admin consoles, internal) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 469.00 Tm
(microservices. Today, getting that data into DuckDB means writing and maintaining a bespoke script per API:) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 455.00 Tm
(handling auth, pagination-adjacent request shaping, and flattening JSON into rows by hand.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 433.00 Tm
(The concrete motivating case: pulling Google Workspace Admin SDK cost and usage reports into DuckDB for) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 419.00 Tm
(analysis. That API - like most REST APIs - needs an authenticated request to a JSON-returning endpoint.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 405.00 Tm
(Nothing about that is Google-specific; the same shape covers GCP billing exports, Stripe, GitHub, or any) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 391.00 Tm
(internal service with an OpenAPI spec.) Tj
/F2 13.50 Tf
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 361.00 Tm
(Proposed Solution) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
54.00 340.00 504.00 0.75 re f
/F1 10.30 Tf
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 321.00 Tm
(rest_ext treats a REST API as an attachable database:) Tj
/F3 8.60 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.220 rg
1 0 0 1 64.00 282.40 Tm
(INSTALL rest_ext;) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 270.19 Tm
(LOAD rest_ext;) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 257.98 Tm
(ATTACH '<config>' AS myapi \(TYPE rest_ext, ...\);) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 245.76 Tm
(SELECT * FROM myapi.<endpoint>\(query_params, body\);) Tj
/F1 10.30 Tf
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 54.00 218.15 Tm
(Three ways to configure an attachment, in increasing order of power:) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 68.00 199.15 Tm
(•) Tj
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 80.00 199.15 Tm
(Single endpoint - just a URL, headers, and method. Produces one bare callable.) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 68.00 180.15 Tm
(•) Tj
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 80.00 180.15 Tm
(Namespace - a hand-written map of name -> URL. Produces one callable per name, dot-qualified) Tj
1 0 0 1 80.00 166.15 Tm
(\(myapi.Users\(...\), myapi.Orders\(...\)\).) Tj
0.110 0.320 0.550 rg
1 0 0 1 68.00 147.15 Tm
(•) Tj
0.140 0.140 0.160 rg
1 0 0 1 80.00 147.15 Tm
(OpenAPI spec-import - point ATTACH at an OpenAPI 2.0 or 3.x document \(a local file or a remote) Tj
1 0 0 1 80.00 133.15 Tm
(SPEC_URL\), and every operation the spec defines becomes a callable automatically, already wired to) Tj
1 0 0 1 80.00 119.15 Tm
(the right URL, method, and path.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 97.15 Tm
(In every mode, the response schema is not fixed up front - it is inferred from the actual JSON returned, at) Tj
1 0 0 1 54.00 83.15 Tm
(query-bind time. A JSON object becomes a STRUCT column, an array becomes a LIST column, and scalars) Tj
/F1 8.00 Tf
0.460 0.460 0.480 rg
1 0 0 1 248.93 30.00 Tm
